      "writtenOn": "2017-05-24T17:03:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ec_host_response.result is already explicitly a uint16_t for this reason.\n\nCross-platform fields must use fixed-size types and must not use enums.  For example, there\u0027s nothing which prevents the compiler from using uint32_t for \u0027enum foo\u0027.\n\nWhere is this actually causing a problem?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 488,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 488,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "3be24cdce152b0fd7160716073e804b09d2569fe",
