      "writtenOn": "2017-05-24T17:30:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, the comment is inaccurate.  It\u0027s talking about the host_cmd_handler_args.result field, not ec_host_response.result.\n\nAnd really, anyone using a result code needs to use uint16_t directly, because there\u0027s no guarantee a result code will be one of the listed codes.  We add new ones periodically.  These are just in an enum rather than separately #defined because it works nicer in debuggers.\n\nI suggest multiple fixes:\n\n1) Change the comment in line 463 to\n/* Host command response codes (16-bit) */\n\n2) You can add EC_RES_MAX, but please comment that status codes should be stored in a uint16_t rather than using enum ec_status directly.\n\n3) Change host_commnand.h to use uint16_t rather than enum ec_status.",
      "parentUuid": "d85651f5_55bec7c1",
